Add PWA file-handling contribution to the web workbench
------------------------------------------------------

Registers a workbench contribution that integrates the Web App
Manifest `file_handlers` launch queue with the editor service:

- Consumes `window.launchQueue` entries launched via the PWA
  "open file" handler (Chrome/Edge on desktop and Android).
- Each launched `FileSystemFileHandle` is registered with the
  browser's `HTMLFileSystemProvider` so it appears as a real
  `file:`-scheme resource that FileEditorInput can open, edit,
  and save back to disk.
- Launched directories open as a workspace folder.
- In browsers without the File System Access API the file
  contents are read and opened as an untitled editor.
- Requests permission to persist the handle so that saving
  back to the launched file works.

The contribution is registered in `workbench.web.main.ts` so it
only loads in the web workbench (not on desktop).

Applies with `git apply` (generated via `git diff --no-index
/dev/null <path>`).

